**How to implement.** The app offers refractiveindex.info over its configured sources folder (.spec-md §0.1: `AppContext.create` composes the library proxies over the configured locations; .spec-md §3.9; the S13.1 brief). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S13.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`: the `compose` that `create` and `recreateLibrary` share (steps 89, 100, 118) builds `catalogueImports` with, beside `exportFolderOpt` and in the same record update, `materialSources = [ MaterialSourceProxy.createRefractiveIndexInfo locations.materialSourcesFolder SourceArchiveDownloader.http ClockProvider.system ]` (steps 446, 447; `ClockProvider.system`, `KitOpening.fs`, step 150). Every other composition (`DefaultStores`, `initWith`, the tests' import contexts) keeps the `[]` of `CatalogueImportContext.create` (step 444). Composing it reads and writes nothing: no folder is created and nothing is downloaded until Update snapshot runs. The record's doc names the sources in no more words. (2) Tests: `AppContextTests` gains `the app scope offers refractiveindex.info over its configured sources folder, holding no snapshot`: `TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName "AppContextTests")`'s `catalogueImports.materialSources` is one source named `refractiveindex.info`, whose `snapshotVersion ()` answers `Ok None`, and nothing exists under the sources folder of `TestAppScope.testLocations (FolderName "AppContextTests")` (step 446). No test runs this source's `updateSnapshot`, so no test reaches the network (.spec-md §8).

**Acceptance.** After the composition, `AppContext.create` MUST compose the refractiveindex.info source over `locations.materialSourcesFolder` with the HTTP seam and every other composition MUST offer none; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the app scope offers refractiveindex.info over its configured sources folder, holding no snapshot`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s43 invariants MUST pass.
